| Versions: a stored program keeps every version it has had. A program kept
| as data (a Home rule, a saved plasmid) is saved, changed, switched off and
| deleted; none of that loses what was there before.
|
| Saving a program that already exists adds a version and makes the one
| before it inactive. Nothing is overwritten. Every version says when it
| was made and whether it is the active one. Deleting makes every version
| inactive: the program stops, and its versions stay readable and can be
| restored. Restoring copies an old version's source into a new active
| version, so history only ever grows.
|
| One version, as it is kept:
|
|   { name, version, source, created_at, active, enabled, broken }
|
| `version` counts from 1 per name; `created_at` is unix seconds; at most one
| version of a name is `active`, and none is once it has been deleted.
| `enabled` (the program's on/off switch) and `broken` (why it will not
| load, "" when it does) are the application's to set, on the active
| version, with `VersionsMark`. Only an active, enabled version should run.
|
| **It keeps nothing itself.** Where a program's versions live (a database
| row, a file, storage) is the application's, and so is loading one. Two
| handlers are the application's to write, and this gene calls both:
|
|   VersionsRead { name } → VersionsHeld { versions }
|       every version of the name, oldest first; [] when there are none
|   VersionsWrite { name, versions } → VersionsWritten
|       keep the whole list for the name, replacing what was kept
|
| Either answers `VersionsFailed { reason }` when the store cannot be
| reached, and the handler that asked answers the same.
|
| Every handler here begins with `Versions`, and so do the application's
| two, because a gene's handlers join the one program-wide table. It needs
| no alias: the time comes from `core`.

| ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
| Saving, restoring
| ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

| A new version of a program, active from now on; the one before it, if
| any, stops being active. `enabled` defaults to true.
VersionsSave { name ∈ String, source ∈ String, enabled ∈ Boolean } =>
    if name ∉ String or name = ""
        return VersionsFailed { reason = "a stored program needs a name" }
    if source ∉ String or source = ""
        return VersionsFailed { reason = "a stored program needs its source" }
    on = true
    if enabled = false, on = false
    emit VersionsRead { name = name } to this get held
    if held ∉ VersionsHeld
        emit VersionsCouldNot { doing = "read", name = name, answer = held } to this get failed
        return failed
    emit Timestamp to core get now
    next = 1
    kept = []
    loop one over held.versions
        if one.version ≥ next, next = one.version + 1
        kept += [one + { active = false }]
    kept += [{ name = name, version = next, source = source, created_at = now.value, active = true, enabled = on, broken = "" }]
    emit VersionsWrite { name = name, versions = kept } to this get wrote
    if wrote ∉ VersionsWritten
        emit VersionsCouldNot { doing = "kept", name = name, answer = wrote } to this get failed
        return failed
    return VersionsSaved { name = name, version = next, created_at = now.value }

| An old version again, as a new active version with that version's
| source. Restoring a deleted program brings it back, switched on.
VersionsRestore { name ∈ String, version ∈ Number } =>
    emit VersionsOne { name = name, version = version } to this get one
    if one ∉ VersionsFound
        return one
    emit VersionsSave { name = name, source = one.record.source, enabled = true } to this get saved
    return saved

| ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
| Reading
| ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

| Every version of a program, oldest first.
VersionsOf { name ∈ String } =>
    emit VersionsRead { name = name } to this get held
    if held ∉ VersionsHeld
        emit VersionsCouldNot { doing = "read", name = name, answer = held } to this get failed
        return failed
    return VersionsList { name = name, items = held.versions }

| One version of a program, by number.
VersionsOne { name ∈ String, version ∈ Number } =>
    emit VersionsRead { name = name } to this get held
    if held ∉ VersionsHeld
        emit VersionsCouldNot { doing = "read", name = name, answer = held } to this get failed
        return failed
    loop one over held.versions
        if one.version = version
            return VersionsFound { record = one }
    return VersionsMissing { name = name, version = version }

| The active version among a program's versions, or null when there is
| none (never saved, or deleted). Asks nothing: an application that read
| many programs at once finds each one's active version with this.
VersionsActiveOf { versions ∈ Array of Any } =>
    if versions ∉ Array
        return VersionsCurrent { record = null }
    loop one over versions
        if one.active = true
            return VersionsCurrent { record = one }
    return VersionsCurrent { record = null }

| ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
| Active and inactive
| ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

| No version is active any more: the program stops. Every version is kept.
| `was` is the version that was active, 0 when none was.
VersionsDeactivate { name ∈ String } =>
    emit VersionsMakeActive { name = name, version = 0 } to this get made
    return made

| Deleting is deactivating: what was written is never thrown away.
VersionsDelete { name ∈ String } =>
    emit VersionsMakeActive { name = name, version = 0 } to this get made
    return made

| One version active again, without a new one: `version`, or the newest
| when it is 0.
VersionsActivate { name ∈ String, version ∈ Number } =>
    emit VersionsRead { name = name } to this get held
    if held ∉ VersionsHeld
        emit VersionsCouldNot { doing = "read", name = name, answer = held } to this get failed
        return failed
    wanted = 0
    if version ∈ Number, wanted = version
    newest = 0
    exists = false
    loop one over held.versions
        if one.version > newest, newest = one.version
        if one.version = wanted, exists = true
    if wanted = 0
        wanted = newest
        exists = newest > 0
    if not exists
        return VersionsMissing { name = name, version = wanted }
    emit VersionsMakeActive { name = name, version = wanted } to this get made
    return made

| Only `version` active, or none when it is 0. Answers
| `VersionsActivated { name, active, was }`.
VersionsMakeActive { name ∈ String, version ∈ Number } =>
    emit VersionsRead { name = name } to this get held
    if held ∉ VersionsHeld
        emit VersionsCouldNot { doing = "read", name = name, answer = held } to this get failed
        return failed
    was = 0
    kept = []
    loop one over held.versions
        if one.active = true, was = one.version
        kept += [one + { active = one.version = version }]
    if was ≠ version
        emit VersionsWrite { name = name, versions = kept } to this get wrote
        if wrote ∉ VersionsWritten
            emit VersionsCouldNot { doing = "kept", name = name, answer = wrote } to this get failed
            return failed
    return VersionsActivated { name = name, active = version, was = was }

| Set `enabled` and/or `broken` on the active version; a field left out is
| left as it is. `VersionsMissing` when no version is active.
VersionsMark { name ∈ String, enabled ∈ Boolean, broken ∈ String } =>
    emit VersionsRead { name = name } to this get held
    if held ∉ VersionsHeld
        emit VersionsCouldNot { doing = "read", name = name, answer = held } to this get failed
        return failed
    marked = null
    kept = []
    loop one over held.versions
        if one.active ≠ true
            kept += [one]
            continue
        changed = one
        if enabled ∈ Boolean, changed = changed + { enabled = enabled }
        if broken ∈ String, changed = changed + { broken = broken }
        marked = changed
        kept += [changed]
    if marked = null
        return VersionsMissing { name = name, version = 0 }
    emit VersionsWrite { name = name, versions = kept } to this get wrote
    if wrote ∉ VersionsWritten
        emit VersionsCouldNot { doing = "kept", name = name, answer = wrote } to this get failed
        return failed
    return VersionsMarked { record = marked }

| The one failure answer: the application's own reason when it gave one.
VersionsCouldNot { doing ∈ String, name ∈ String, answer ∈ Any } =>
    reason = "the versions of '$name' could not be $doing"
    if answer ∈ VersionsFailed and answer.reason ∈ String, reason = answer.reason
    return VersionsFailed { reason = reason }
